  "modelingNotes": [
    "Soldiers' and Sailors' Memorial Arch, Grand Army Plaza, Brooklyn. Procedural CC0 geometry, styled to STYLE.md. bun generators/soldiers-sailors-arch.ts",
    "Map frame: x = passage axis (+x is the park/south face, which carries the Army and Navy groups), y = the long facade, z = up. Placement in the catalog: 40.6729891, -73.9699033; bearing 81; elevation 0.",
    "The footprint is the OSM envelope: masonry x ±3.85, y -11.7..11.8, with the paired-column bays reaching x ±5.4. That envelope is 0.05 m off-centre in y, so the model is built symmetric about y = 0 and shifted by +0.05 at the end, which keeps the bounds and origin exactly where they were. Reference: https://s-media.nyc.gov/agencies/lpc/lp/0821.pdf",
    "Original procedural model from https://github.com/alexwohlbruck/landmarks (catalog id \"soldiers-sailors-arch\", model \"soldiers-sailors-arch\"), generated by https://github.com/alexwohlbruck/landmarks/blob/c3921f733df14b41e1f6d15853cce7b343886f17/generators/soldiers-sailors-arch.ts. That repository is the editable source; source.blend.gz is the exported mesh imported into Blender for convenience.",
    "Exported for Open Landmarks v1: placement bearing and scale baked in; moving parts frozen in their rest pose; footings and basements below the lowest ground (y = 0) cut away; material colours carried over exactly, as library finishes where they are not standard swatches."
  ],
